---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  locale="en"
  title="Monessor — Fractional CTO, Tech Strategy & Regulatory Governance"
  description="Executive advisory firm led by Alex Turcotte, specializing in technology strategy, AI integration, fractional CTO services, and IT governance for regulated sectors."
>
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css" />

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Executive practice • Strategic technology leadership</p>
        <h1>Clarity. Governance. Execution.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Monessor supports organizations facing complex technology challenges—digital transformation,
          artificial intelligence, platform modernization—by providing senior, pragmatic leadership
          focused on concrete outcomes.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-synthesis hero-synthesis--desktop" aria-hidden="false">
          Monessor is engaged when technology and product become strategic issues and executive trade-offs
          are no longer clear. The objective is to restore a sustainable trajectory without compromising
          stability, compliance, or impact.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-synthesis hero-synthesis--mobile" aria-hidden="true">
          Monessor is engaged when technology and product become strategic and clear executive trade-offs are required.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-detail">
          Working alongside executive teams, Monessor clarifies priorities and trade-offs across product,
          technology, and risk while stabilizing critical platforms and guiding modernization efforts to
          translate technology decisions into durable business results.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a class="btn" href="#contact">Get in touch</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#situations">View situations</a>
        </div>

        <div class="microproof">
          <div class="pill">Montreal</div>
          <div class="pill">Quebec & Canada</div>
          <div class="pill">Complex environments</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SITUATIONS -->
  <section class="section" id="situations">
    <div class="container max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2>Areas of intervention</h2>
      <p class="sublead">
        When technology becomes a strategic, operational, or governance issue.
      </p>

      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Platforms under strain</h3>
          <p>Critical systems, technical debt and unpredictable delivery.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Artificial Intelligence & Automation</h3>
          <p>Evaluating AI/ML opportunities, building business cases, and strategic integration in regulated environments.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Modernization</h3>
          <p>Legacy → target trajectory, cost / risk / value trade-offs.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Governance & decisions</h3>
          <p>Aligning executive leadership, IT and risk.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="useful">
    <div class="container max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2>When Monessor creates the most value</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <p>
            When technology has become critical to the organization, but priorities,
            risks and accountabilities are no longer clearly aligned.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p>
            When a core platform needs to be modernized without compromising stability,
            regulatory compliance or stakeholder trust.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p>
            When an organization wants to evaluate the potential of artificial intelligence and
            automation, ensuring investments are driven by solid business cases rather than hype.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p>
            When teams are working hard, yet real impact is difficult to measure or
            clearly articulate at the executive level.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p>
            When persistent tension exists between product, technology and operations,
            without a clear framework for trade-off decisions.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p>
            When an organization needs senior technology and product leadership,
            without immediately hiring a full-time CTO or CPTO.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SERVICES -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="services">
    <div class="container max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2>Services</h2>

      <div class="trust-badges">
        <div class="badge">
          <div class="badge-value">20+</div>
          <div class="badge-label">Years of senior technology leadership</div>
        </div>
        <div class="badge">
          <div class="badge-value">Pragmatic</div>
          <div class="badge-label">Results-oriented executive approach</div>
        </div>
        <div class="badge">
          <div class="badge-value">100%</div>
          <div class="badge-label">Delivery by seasoned expert consortium</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-container">
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <button class="accordion-trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="service-1-content">
            <span>Fractional CTO</span>
            <svg class="accordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
          <div class="accordion-content" id="service-1-content">
            <p class="accordion-text">
              Senior technology leadership embedded within your executive team to align product roadmap with business objectives. We guide 30–60–90 day planning, crisis management, and technical team stabilization without the cost of a full-time executive.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">
          <button class="accordion-trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="service-2-content">
            <span>Strategy &amp; Governance</span>
            <svg class="accordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
          <div class="accordion-content" id="service-2-content">
            <p class="accordion-text">
              Translating business vision into robust and secure architectures. We design the decision-making frameworks needed to navigate highly regulated environments (BSIF / OSFI), optimize team structure, and architect AI and automation initiatives.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">
          <button class="accordion-trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="service-3-content">
            <span>Platform Modernization</span>
            <svg class="accordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
          <div class="accordion-content" id="service-3-content">
            <p class="accordion-text">
              Pragmatic <em>build vs. buy</em> arbitrage, legacy technical debt reduction, and platform viability assessment. We secure migration trajectories to minimize operational risk and maximize return on your technology investments.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- APPROACH -->
  <section class="section" id="approach">
    <div class="container max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2>Approach</h2>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <p class="step-num">01</p>
          <h3>Clarify</h3>
          <p>Issues, constraints, risks and structuring decisions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <p class="step-num">02</p>
          <h3>Structure</h3>
          <p>Options, trajectory, governance and prioritization.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <p class="step-num">03</p>
          <h3>Execute</h3>
          <p>Execution support and leadership.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="note">
        <p><strong>What Monessor is not:</strong> a development agency or a buzzword factory.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ABOUT -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="about">
    <div class="container max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2>Practice leadership</h2>
      <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 20px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 24px;">Alex Turcotte, Managing Partner</h3>

      <div class="about">
        <div>
          <p class="lead">
            Alex Turcotte leads the Monessor practice as a CTO / CPTO for executive teams navigating complex
            technology, product, and organizational challenges. The practice combines senior leadership with
            an agile ecosystem of specialists to structure and deliver mandates with rigor.
          </p>
          <p>
            Drawing on more than twenty years of experience at the intersection of technology, product, and governance,
            Alex works primarily in organizations where platforms are critical, regulatory constraints are significant,
            and technology decisions are tightly linked to business outcomes. The role is to bring clarity where complexity has accumulated:
            unclear priorities, misunderstood technical debt, tensions between short-term delivery and long-term sustainability,
            or the evaluation of artificial intelligence and automation opportunities in settings where compliance and governance are non-negotiable.
          </p>
          <p>
            Between 2018 and 2021, Alex held product leadership roles as Product Lead and Squad Lead, with full responsibility for defining,
            delivering, and scaling digital products used by key participants in financial markets. That experience continues to shape his approach:
            technology only creates value when it serves clear, shared, and well-understood use cases.
          </p>
          <p>
            He is known for a calm, structured, and pragmatic leadership style, particularly useful in contexts of transition,
            modernization, or constrained growth. Monessor draws on a network of seasoned experts and specialized partners to mobilize the
            right capabilities according to the nature and scale of the challenge.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-box">
          <div class="hero-card">
            <div class="portrait">
              <img src="/assets/alex.jpg" alt="Alex Turcotte" />
            </div>
            <div class="hero-card-body">
              <p class="name">Alex Turcotte</p>
              <p class="title">Founder - Monessor</p>
              <p class="small">
                Fractional CTO and executive advisor in technology strategy, platform modernization, and IT governance.
              </p>
              <br />
              <div class="hero-card-links">
                <a class="libutton" href="https://www.linkedin.com/comm/mynetwork/discovery-see-all?usecase=PEOPLE_FOLLOWS&amp;followMember=turcottealex" target="_blank">Follow on LinkedIn</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTACT -->
  <section class="section" id="contact">
    <div class="container max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="sublead">
        Tell us what you are trying to accomplish and where it is blocking you.
        A response will be provided quickly.
      </p>

      <div class="contact-box">
        <div class="contact-actions">
          <a id="email-button" class="btn" href="#" aria-label="Send an email">
            Send an email
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="https://calendar.app.google/jrWp3LMihMCr5qew7" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Schedule a meeting">
            Schedule a meeting
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="small contact-meta contact-meta--phone">
          <span class="contact-label">Phone:</span>
          <span class="contact-value"><span class="phone-secure" aria-label="Phone number">Call</span></span>
        </p>
        <p class="small contact-meta">
          <span class="contact-label">Or directly:</span>
          <a id="email-link-2" class="contact-value" href="#" aria-label="Email address">
            <span data-user="info" data-domain="monessor" data-tld="com">Contact</span>
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <footer class="footer">
        <p class="small footer-line">© <span id="year"></span> Monessor Consulting Services Inc. <span class="footer-separator" aria-hidden="true"> | </span> <span class="contact-label">Phone:</span> <span class="contact-value"><span class="phone-secure" aria-label="Phone number">Call</span></span></p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script slot="scripts" src="/scripts/main.js"></script>
</Layout>
